WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:29.792
Woah!

2
00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:34.168
-[chocking]
-[rope creaking, swinging]

3
00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:40.270
[struggling, choking]

4
00:00:42.512 --> 00:00:45.800
Ay, no, no, no, [crying] no,

5
00:00:46.568 --> 00:00:50.664
[elongating] No!

6
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.750
["no" fading]

7
00:01:03.328 --> 00:01:04.664
[struggling, gasping]

8
00:01:05.296 --> 00:01:07.120
[panting]

9
00:01:11.848 --> 00:01:12.938
[moans]

10
00:01:15.648 --> 00:01:17.167
[wheezes]

11
00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.042
[wheezes]

12
00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.313
[struggling softly]

13
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.542
[grunting loudly]

14
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.250
[breathes out, gasps]

15
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:31.125
[grunting]

16
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.083
[grunting, wheezing]

17
00:01:35.885 --> 00:01:38.917
[wheezing in pain]

18
00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:56.956
[panting]

19
00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:04.000
[panting]

20
00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.889
[groans, wheezes]

21
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.300
[man] Excuse me?

22
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.000
Excuse me, sir?

23
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.500
Excuse me?

24
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
[sheep] Oh, come on.

25
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.042
[man] Do you have a moment, sir?

26
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:34.958
[sheep] I'm kind of in the middle
of something here.

27
00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:37.000
Yes? Thank you.

28
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.326
I've come a long way for you, Franck.

29
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.000
My name is Victor.

30
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Hi.

31
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.125
And you are…

32
00:02:57.813 --> 00:02:59.500
You are Franck.

33
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.000
You are so much more than just a sheep,
aren't you?

34
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Oh yeah? How would you know?

35
00:03:10.346 --> 00:03:12.750
Look at you. You're an adventurer, Franck.

36
00:03:13.958 --> 00:03:16.750
Just like me, you're... a lone wolf.

37
00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:21.750
Tell me, does one choose to be alone?

38
00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:25.080
No, one doesn't.

39
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.750
One doesn't even choose to be a wolf.

40
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.000
Or does one?

41
00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.750
Well, mister, err… Hector…

42
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:39.875
Victor, Victor.

43
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.833
I don't know what you're on about,

44
00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:45.333
but I'm just a sheep
minding its own business.

45
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.600
And I suggest you do the same.

46
00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.542
No. No, no, no, Franck. Wait, wait, wait.

47
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.125
No. This is not...

48
00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:54.500
 the way.

49
00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:57.270
Just give me one minute
of your precious time.

50
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.417
"Precious time"? [laughs mockingly]

51
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.170
-Yeah, just give me one minute.
-[sighs]

52
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.708
You would have one more minute,
wouldn't you?

53
00:04:08.346 --> 00:04:11.583
Okay, half. Half a minute.

54
00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:17.917
-[gulls calling]
-[ocean waves crashing faintly]

55
00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:24.008
[sighs]

56
00:04:25.471 --> 00:04:29.375
I knew it. I knew it.

57
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.583
You will not regret this.

58
00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:34.583
The adventures you will have,

59
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.958
all the lives you've ever wanted,

60
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.625
all you've been missing.

61
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:46.000
Here. This is the best product
we have in store.

62
00:04:47.073 --> 00:04:49.917
Variable spin speed,
excellent tumble performance,

63
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.458
in one... handy... device. Squeaky clean!

64
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.250
Well, this... this better be good.

65
00:05:01.311 --> 00:05:03.917
Took me ages to tie that rope.

66
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.250
With my fucking hooves.

67
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.083
No more need for hooves.

68
00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.583
No more sheepy business.

69
00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:11.708
[timer going off]

70
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.667
-Ho! Time flies.
-Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

71
00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:21.042
How does this thing work?
I mean, how do I make it work?

72
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:21.875
No you don't.

73
00:05:22.537 --> 00:05:23.960
I just turned it on for you.

74
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.250
When can I go?

75
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.333
-Where can I go?
-We will pick you up.

76
00:05:31.417 --> 00:05:33.583
Don't worry, just stay here.

77
00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:34.854
In this exact place.

78
00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:37.134
Don't move. Just wait.

79
00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.208
That's it?

80
00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:41.771
Hey!

81
00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.208
Hey!

82
00:05:44.292 --> 00:05:50.310
Wait, mister, eh, Casper,
eh, Hector, whatever!

83
00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.917
[no audio playing on headphones]

84
00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.042
[distorted, high-pitched audio playing]

85
00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:15.000
-[gulls calling]
-[ocean waves crashing faintly]

86
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.458
[skips track]

87
00:06:29.542 --> 00:06:30.792
[fast-forwarding]

88
00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.208
[hopeful music playing]

89
00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.004
[thunder rumbling faintly]

90
00:06:47.003 --> 00:06:47.917
[thunder rumbling]

91
00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.167
[stopwatch ticking]

92
00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.750
[device ticking synchronously]

93
00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.238
[faint rumbling]

94
00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:46.950
[music continues playing]

95
00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:09.729
[music climaxing]
[vocalizing]

96
00:08:21.063 --> 00:08:23.170
[vocalizing continues]

97
00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:34.985
[music softening]

98
00:08:39.729 --> 00:08:41.000
[music stops]

99
00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:46.545
[gasps]

100
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.155
[panting]

101
00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.188
Huh… huh?

102
00:08:58.292 --> 00:08:59.830
Huh?!

103
00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.240
[rubbing and squeaking]

104
00:09:08.188 --> 00:09:11.750
[ambient peaceful nature sounds]

105
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.925
[motor running]

106
00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.930
[washing machine motor sound faints]

107
00:09:52.165 --> 00:09:54.020
[washer's door shuts]

108
00:09:58.540 --> 00:09:59.706
[timer goes off]

109
00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:06.420
[hopeful music playing softly]
